James Rising sought assistance in drafting a response to an email regarding potential supervision of a student in various academic programs. He outlined the relevant programs, their transitions, and funding statuses. Key points included the transition of the Master's in Marine Policy to the Environmental Science & Management program with a Marine track, the suitability of the Ph.D. in Marine Policy for non-traditional students, and the self-funded nature of the ESM and Environmental Economics Master's programs. James emphasized directing the applicant to a new form for program identification. The final outcome identified that the email received contained no specific questions and merely stated the sender was not taking students, suggesting a brief acknowledgment was sufficient for a response.
